# Moving over and between folds.

=== j moves over a closed fold as one line
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When the cursor is already on a folded line, it moves to the next unfolded line or the next closed fold.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>jj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five

=== k onto a closed fold lands on its first line
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When moving the cursor upwards or downwards and when scrolling, the cursor will move to the first line of a sequence of folded lines.
given:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>k
expect:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
  five

=== a count of j counts a closed fold once
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When the cursor is already on a folded line, it moves to the next unfolded line or the next closed fold.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>2j
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six

=== j from one closed fold to the next
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When the cursor is already on a folded line, it moves to the next unfolded line or the next closed fold.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :1,2fold<CR>:3,4fold<CR>jj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five

=== G into a closed fold leaves it closed
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  jump far jumps: "G", "gg", etc.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>Gk
expect:
  |one
  two
  three
  four

=== G keeps the cursor on the last line of a closed fold
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  While the cursor is on folded lines, the cursor is always displayed in the first column.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>G
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four

=== {count}G into the middle of a closed fold
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  jump far jumps: "G", "gg", etc.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>3Gj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five

=== gg into a closed fold leaves it closed
ref:    options.txt *'foldopen'*
quote:  jump far jumps: "G", "gg", etc.
given:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
keys:   :1,2fold<CR>ggj
expect:
  one
  two
  |three
  four

=== :{number} into a closed fold leaves it closed
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When the cursor is already on a folded line, it moves to the next unfolded line or the next closed fold.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>:3<CR>j
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five

=== w stops once on a closed fold
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  Many movement commands handle a sequence of folded lines like an empty line. For example, the "w" command stops once in the first column.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>w
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five

=== zj moves to the start of the next fold
ref:    fold.txt *zj*
quote:  Move downwards to the start of the next fold.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>zozj
expect:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five

=== zj counts a closed fold as one fold
ref:    fold.txt *zj*
quote:  A closed fold is counted as one fold.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zj
expect:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
  five
  six

=== zj enters a nested open fold
ref:    fold.txt *zj*
quote:  Move downwards to the start of the next fold.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zRzjzj
expect:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six

=== zj with a count
ref:    fold.txt *zj*
quote:  When a count is used, repeats the command [count] times.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>:5,6fold<CR>zR2zj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six

=== zj with no fold below does not move
ref:    fold.txt *zj*
quote:  Move downwards to the start of the next fold.
given:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
keys:   :1,2fold<CR>zj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four

=== zk moves to the end of the previous fold
ref:    fold.txt *zk*
quote:  Move upwards to the end of the previous fold.
given:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>zRzk
expect:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five

=== zk with a count
ref:    fold.txt *zk*
quote:  When a count is used, repeats the command [count] times.
given:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  |six
keys:   :1,2fold<CR>:4,5fold<CR>zR2zk
expect:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
  five
  six

=== dzj deletes to the start of the next fold
ref:    fold.txt *zj*
quote:  This command can be used after an |operator|.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>zRdzj
expect:
  |three
  four
  five

=== [z moves to the start of the open fold
ref:    fold.txt *[z*
quote:  Move to the start of the current open fold.
given:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
  five
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>zo[z
expect:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
  five

=== [z at the start moves to the containing fold's start
ref:    fold.txt *[z*
quote:  If already at the start, move to the start of the fold that contains it.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zO[z
expect:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
  five
  six

=== [z with no containing fold does not move
ref:    fold.txt *[z*
quote:  If there is no containing fold, the command fails.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>zo[z
expect:
  one
  |two
  three
  four

=== ]z moves to the end of the open fold
ref:    fold.txt *]z*
quote:  Move to the end of the current open fold.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>zo]z
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
  five

=== ]z at the end moves to the containing fold's end
ref:    fold.txt *]z*
quote:  If already at the end, move to the end of the fold that contains it.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zO]z]z
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six

=== 2]z repeats
ref:    fold.txt *]z*
quote:  When a count is used, repeats the command [count] times.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
  five
  six
keys:   :3,4fold<CR>:2,5fold<CR>zO2]z
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  four
  |five
  six

=== d]z is an exclusive motion
ref:    fold.txt *]z*
quote:  Move to the end of the current open fold.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>zojd]z
expect:
  one
  two
  |four
  five

=== zj is a jump
ref:    fold.txt *zj*
quote:  Move downwards to the start of the next fold.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>zj
expect:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
jumps:  1:0

=== [z is a jump
ref:    fold.txt *[z*
quote:  Move to the start of the current open fold.
given:
  one
  two
  |three
  four
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>zo[z
expect:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
jumps:  3:0

=== j over a closed fold is not a jump
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When the cursor is already on a folded line, it moves to the next unfolded line or the next closed fold.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>jj
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
jumps:
